\define engine(title, icon, text)
<div class="tv-engine">
<div class="tv-engine-head">{{$icon$}} <$link to="$title$">$title$</$link></div>

$text$

<div class="tv-engine-open"><$link to="$title$">Open the demo →</$link></div>
</div>
\end

TiddlyVisuals is a collection of ''engines for [[TW5-Graph|Graph]]'', the graphing plugin for TiddlyWiki by [[Flibbles]]. <<.graph>> collects tiddlers and their connections as nodes and edges; an engine decides how they look and how you work with them. The engines here show the same tiddlers in new ways, and every change you make on a board is written back to the tiddlers.

<div class="tv-engines">

<<engine "Pinboard" "$:/core/images/layout-button" "An infinite canvas: tiddlers become cards you place freely, connect by dragging from card to card, and surround with drawings, sticky notes and frames. A path of frames and cards plays back as a presentation.">>

<<engine "Kanban" "$:/core/images/list-bullet" "Columns and swimlanes from the fields of your tiddlers. Dragging a card to another column rewrites its fields; arrows between cards show what blocks what.">>

</div>

!! Installing

{{Install pills}}

Then pick the engine's template in a graph's settings. Each demo page explains the details.

!! TW5-Graph itself

[[Graph]] is Flibbles' own page for <<.graph>>, with its [[Documentation]] and the [[Vis-Network]] engine. TiddlyVisuals builds on it and keeps it as it is.

